$MDESC::Type = "TAC";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> TAC Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Avicord's Planet" @
         "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Warm Summer Air" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> After Sunset" @ 
         "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> H.A.L.O. High Altitude, Low Opening. The term is from the ancient days but the same principle applies. Jump high to avoid detection and hit your jets and start firing before they know what's coming. The flag bases have heavy missile defences so doing a H.A.L.O. run is the about the safest way in. Once in the generator is easily smashed to knock out the missile turrets giving you a safe exit path. In the middle of the map you will find the Pulse sensor control. Not only does this give you 5 points it gives you access to the high altitude pulse sensors over both bases making it vital for both score and early warning of incoming HALO attacks. The first team to reach 30 points shall be the victor!" @
         "\n\n<f1>For the TAC Mod:<f0> www.tribes-universe.com/tac/" @
	 "\n\n<f1>Map designed by:<f0> [TPG]SaNTa[DTM]";